{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00731",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 2.31,
      "end_seconds": 16.84,
      "duration_seconds": 14.53,
      "text": "Morning. Spring's started and my eyes are streaming, itching, the lot. I want my usual sorted before it gets bad, so can we go through it quickly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.74,
      "end_seconds": 25.27,
      "duration_seconds": 5.53,
      "text": "Of course. Tell me what you're using at the moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.88,
      "end_seconds": 45.92,
      "duration_seconds": 18.04,
      "text": "Olopatadine eye drops, twice a day. Cetirizine, 10 mg, once a day. Fluticasone nasal spray, two sprays once a day. And montelukast, 10 mg, maybe? At night? I take it for the asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.0,
      "end_seconds": 54.59,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "And is the montelukast 10 mg? You said maybe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 58.19,
      "end_seconds": 66.27,
      "duration_seconds": 8.08,
      "text": "It's 10, I'm fairly sure. It might be 5. I'd have to check the box."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.48,
      "end_seconds": 77.0,
      "duration_seconds": 7.52,
      "text": "I'll check the record, that's fine. Which of those is working best? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.09,
      "end_seconds": 90.06,
      "duration_seconds": 8.97,
      "text": "The cetirizine, and the eye drops. The nasal spray I use when I remember. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.46,
      "end_seconds": 98.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.57,
      "text": "How have your eyes been this week? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.69,
      "end_seconds": 109.74,
      "duration_seconds": 9.05,
      "text": "Itchy and watery, but not red. I can cope. I'd just like to be ahead of it. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.62,
      "end_seconds": 119.66,
      "duration_seconds": 7.04,
      "text": "Sensible. And your wider health, what do you have on the record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.72,
      "end_seconds": 129.08,
      "duration_seconds": 6.36,
      "text": "Hay fever, obviously, asthma, since I was a child, and eczema. Classic trio."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.27,
      "end_seconds": 134.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "Any operations?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.34,
      "end_seconds": 142.83,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "A squint operation, when I was four."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.03,
      "end_seconds": 151.64,
      "duration_seconds": 5.61,
      "text": "Thank you. How's your asthma at the moment? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.54,
      "end_seconds": 162.66,
      "duration_seconds": 8.12,
      "text": "Quiet. Spring and summer tend to be when it kicks in, but it's fine now. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.67,
      "end_seconds": 177.42,
      "duration_seconds": 11.75,
      "text": "Good. Here's what I suggest, given the season. Start the nasal spray now, every day, rather than occasionally, because it works by building up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.38,
      "end_seconds": 183.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Right. I've been inconsistent. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.75,
      "end_seconds": 198.57,
      "duration_seconds": 11.82,
      "text": "And start the cetirizine and the eye drops a week before your worst weeks, if you can predict them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.09,
      "end_seconds": 204.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "Mid-May usually. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.11,
      "end_seconds": 221.2,
      "duration_seconds": 14.09,
      "text": "Then start in early May. Keep windows closed in the morning, shower when you get in, and wipe your eyes with a cool damp cloth."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 225.03,
      "end_seconds": 228.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "I do all that, mostly. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.04,
      "end_seconds": 238.65,
      "duration_seconds": 6.61,
      "text": "Wear wraparound sunglasses, it keeps pollen off your eyes. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 242.38,
      "end_seconds": 247.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "I've got some, in the car. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.03,
      "end_seconds": 259.48,
      "duration_seconds": 9.45,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in six weeks, to see how the season's going and check your asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 263.55,
      "end_seconds": 267.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Six weeks. Right, thank you. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.25,
      "end_seconds": 276.46,
      "duration_seconds": 6.21,
      "text": "You're welcome. Do you want the reminder in writing? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 279.22,
      "end_seconds": 283.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "Yes, please, on the prescription slip. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.02,
      "end_seconds": 291.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.48,
      "text": "I'll print it with the repeat prescriptions. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 294.47,
      "end_seconds": 297.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Marvellous. Same drugs, nothing new? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 300.43,
      "end_seconds": 306.01,
      "duration_seconds": 5.58,
      "text": "Nothing new, just using them in a smarter order. ~"
    }
  ]
}
